## 2. Native libraries bundled inside wheels

Versions below are those in the wheels used for the Linux ARM64 / CPython 3.12
AgentCore runtime. File lists and license texts were re-checked against the
wheels installed in `backend/.venv` (pikepdf and Pillow: Linux x86_64 wheels
with the same library set; pypdfium2: the `py3-none` wheel whose bundled
license data is under `licenses/data/linux_x64/BUILD_LICENSES`, with the same
component list as the ARM64 build).

### 2.1 pikepdf 10.17.0

| Component | Where | License (SPDX) | Source of the license text |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| qpdf 12.4.x (`pikepdf.__libqpdf_version__`) | `pikepdf.libs/libqpdf-*.so.30.4.2` | Apache-2.0 | wheel `licenses/third-party-licenses/qpdf.txt` |
| libjpeg-turbo 1.5.3 (AlmaLinux 8 build, per wheel SBOM `sboms/auditwheel.cdx.json`) | `pikepdf.libs/libjpeg-*.so.62.2.0` | IJG AND BSD-3-Clause AND Zlib | wheel `licenses/third-party-licenses/libjpeg-turbo.txt`, `libjpeg-turbo-README.ijg.txt` |
| zlib, libstdc++, libgcc_s | not bundled; system libraries of the runtime environment | n/a | n/a |

Other files shipped in the pikepdf wheel (not native libraries used by this project):
`GPL-3.0.txt` and `GCC-exception-3.1.txt` apply only to GCC runtime libraries
in musllinux wheels (per the wheel's `third-party-licenses/README.md`); the
manylinux wheel used here contains no such library. Data files
`verapdf_rules.json` (CC-BY-4.0), `sRGB.icc` (Zlib) and `_latin_enc.py` (MIT)
are data only; this project does not call the PDF/A functions.

